@startuml
' UC05.1 - Đăng nhập bằng Google
autonumber "<b>0.</b> "
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor white
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor white
skinparam BoundaryBackgroundColor white
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBackgroundColor white
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor black
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor black
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam MaxMessageSize 200

' UC05.1 from docs/source-of-truth/LearnUP_UseCase.docx, row 8.
' BR-35/36/37/38/39 read from LearnUP_QuyTacNghiepVu.docx.
' Scope: the unavailable fallback selected by the inspected local frontend configuration.
' UI page: frontend/src/pages/guest/login.tsx:157/241-244 (LoginPage).
' Button: frontend/src/components/guest/google.sign.in.tsx:53-61 (GoogleSignIn).
' Config: frontend/src/services/google.identity.ts:33-34 (googleClientId).
' Message: frontend/src/utils/google.sign.in.ts:9-13 (GOOGLE_UNAVAILABLE_MESSAGE).
' No nonblank VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in frontend/.env files or the current process.
' frontend/.env.example:38 also has an empty value; vite.config.ts supplies no replacement ID.
' Precondition: Guest is on /login, ordinary form loading=false, Google client ID absent.
' Intended permitted account roles are Organizer/Instructor/Learner; the caller is still Guest.
' !clientId causes the Google loader effect to return without loading the GIS script.
' GoogleSignIn renders a fallback button; click calls onError(GOOGLE_UNAVAILABLE_MESSAGE).
' LoginPage supplies onError=setError; its existing Alert renders the error description.
' This deterministic fallback needs no alt/opt, Google lifeline, API Gateway or database.
' hide footbox is retained as explicitly requested; the known draw.io converter may ignore it.

actor "Guest" as Guest
boundary "Login Page" as Screen

activate Guest
Guest -> Screen : Click Continue with Google
activate Screen
Screen -->> Guest : Google sign-in is currently unavailable.\nPlease sign in with your email and password.
deactivate Screen
deactivate Guest

' Google authentication IS implemented elsewhere in current source; it is not reached here.
' Configured branch: GoogleSignIn initializes GIS in popup mode and receives a credential.
' LoginPage.googleSubmit:71 -> identity.service.ts:32 googleLoginAPI -> POST /api/v1/auth/google.
' AuthController invokes GoogleSignInService.signIn; GoogleIdTokenVerifier validates the ID token.
' GoogleSignInService:47 looks up the verified email with UserRepository.findByEmailForUpdate.
' It rejects absent accounts, ADMIN, disabled credentials and denied Tenant sign-in access.
' Tenant access includes non-deleted/active account, Organization and Subscription checks.
' Allowed credentials lead to AuthService.issueSession, without automatic account creation.
' These implemented branches, and their API/DB/role errors, are not executed by this local UI path.
' Therefore the AS-IS gap is Google sign-in not configured/available in the inspected build,
' not Google authentication not implemented. Other deployed build configuration is unverified.
' No redirect, callback, token exchange/verification, account lookup, session creation,
' role/tenant check or DB/cross-service request is asserted for the fallback click.
' Excluded: password login execution, registration, activation, recovery and enterprise SSO.
' The password suggestion is displayed text only; no UC05 password request is initiated.
@enduml
